TEST: wifi: ath11k: guard the extension descriptor frames against a firmware divert

After a station associates the firmware releases buffer ids it never owned,
with addresses that match no queued buffer. Each part has its own module
parameter, read for each frame, default on:

ext_sg_tcp_only sends a frame with fragments through an extension descriptor
only if it is plain IPv4 or IPv6 TCP; any other is made linear. The refusals
are counted by reason in soc_dp_stats.

ext_after_compl holds every extension descriptor frame to a station, TSO
batch or scatter-gather, until the hardware has completed one frame of it on
the normal path. The flag is in ath11k_sta, which is cleared when the station
is added. The held frames are counted.

ext_log_first logs the first 8 frames of each station sent through extension
descriptors, with the time since the station was added.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
